        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_check" kindref="compound">Check</ref> if an image is compatible with current system&apos;s environment. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The system environment is given as a &apos;target-id&apos; which has the form:</para>
<para>&lt;target-id&gt; := &lt;processor&gt; ( &quot;:&quot; &lt;target-feature&gt; ( &quot;+&quot; | &quot;-&quot; ) )*</para>
<para>If a feature is not specific as &apos;+&apos; or &apos;-&apos; it is assumed to be in an &apos;any&apos; and is compatible with either &apos;+&apos; or &apos;-&apos;. The HSA runtime returns this information using the target-id, while we use the <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_e_l_f" kindref="compound">ELF</ref> header to determine these features. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
